#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# farey_sequence

#% text
# `farey_sequence(k)` gives the Farey sequence of order `k`: the fractions in `[0, 1]` with denominator at most `k`, in increasing order; `farey_sequence(k, j)` gives its `j`-th term.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
farey_sequence(5)
#% output
#= [0, 1/5, 1/4, 1/3, 2/5, 1/2, 3/5, 2/3, 3/4, 4/5, 1]

#% cell
farey_sequence(24, 17)
#% output
#= 2/21

#% cell
length(farey_sequence(15))
#% output
#= 73

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `euler_phi`, `continued_fraction`
